# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# History: this file previously set `Cache-Control: no-store` on `/*`. That was
# there for one reason - Navy NMCI's web proxy ignored `must-revalidate` and
# pinned a weeks-old copy of the Calculator, and `no-store` is the only
# directive such a proxy respects. Supporting those networks was dropped in
# August 2026, so the blanket no-store went with it: it forbade the browser
# HTTP cache and Cloudflare's edge from holding anything, for every visitor,
# to solve a problem nobody here has any more.
#
# The split below is the ordinary one. Two groups, decided by a single
# question: does the URL change when the file does?
#
#   - Assets referenced with ?v=N are immutable AT THAT URL. Bumping the
#     version makes it a different URL, which is a fresh fetch, so they can be
#     cached for a year. That is the point of the ?v= convention already in
#     use here, and until now nothing took advantage of it.
#   - Everything else - HTML, and the handful of files referenced with no
#     version - must revalidate, or a deploy would not reach anyone.
#
# `no-cache` does NOT mean "do not cache". It means "store it, but check with
# the server before reusing it", which gives cheap 304s rather than full
# re-downloads. `no-store` is the one that forbids keeping a copy at all.

# Default: revalidate on every use. This deliberately covers HTML, and also
# theme.js, manifest.json and search-index.json, which are all requested
# WITHOUT a ?v= and so would go stale if cached. search-index.json in
# particular is rewritten every time a polymer is added.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# The service worker decides when every other cached file is replaced, so it
# must never be stale itself. Called out separately from the default so it
# cannot be swept into a long-lived rule by a later edit.
#
# NOTE: this rule does not currently take effect. The zone's Browser Cache TTL
# is set to 4 hours, and that setting RAISES any shorter freshness the origin
# asks for - so `no-cache` here comes back as `max-age=14400`, while
# style.css's year is respected because it is longer. Verified against the
# deployed site: sw.js and theme.js returned max-age=14400 with
# cf-cache-status REVALIDATED, everything else obeyed this file.
#
# Two mitigations are in place, so nothing is actually stale: theme.js is now
# versioned like every other asset, and every page registers the worker with
# updateViaCache: "none", which makes the browser fetch sw.js bypassing its
# HTTP cache entirely. The rule is kept because it becomes correct the moment
# Browser Cache TTL is set to "Respect Existing Headers" in the Cloudflare
# dashboard (Caching -> Configuration), which is the real fix.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# Live data. Caching /api/health would break the deployment check, and caching
# /api/recognize would hand one person's result to the next visitor.
/api/*
  Cache-Control: no-store

# Versioned in the URL - safe to keep for a year. Every reference to these
# carries ?v=N, so a change to the file is always a change to the URL. Path
# matching here ignores the query string, which is what makes this work: the
# rule applies to whichever ?v= is current.
/style.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/nav.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/app.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/polymer-calc-core.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/polymer-data.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/polymer-graph.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/polymer-search.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/superatoms.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/ocr-decoders.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/thermal-library.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/chain-data.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The vendored RDKit build (6.9 MB of WebAssembly, the largest thing served
# here) deliberately has NO rule, and inherits `no-cache` from /* above.
#
# Not for want of trying. A `/vendor/*` rule came back MERGED with /* as
# `no-cache, public, max-age=2592000`, and rewriting it as two exact paths
# changed nothing - still merged, and cf-cache-status DYNAMIC, so not a stale
# edge copy either. The root-level rules above override /* cleanly, so
# something about these files (subdirectory, or the application/wasm type
# Cloudflare does not edge-cache) makes them concatenate instead. Since
# no-cache wins that merge, the rule bought nothing but a contradictory
# header, so it is gone.
#
# What it costs: one conditional request per session, answered 304 with no
# body - not a 6.9 MB re-download. The service worker caches the file
# outright and serves it without touching the network at all, so this only
# affects a first visit or a cold worker. Judged not worth further deploys.
#
# If RDKit is ever upgraded, give it a ?v= and add it to the immutable list
# above; a versioned root-relative URL is the pattern that demonstrably works.
